# Summon: Esper Maduin through all three chapters. Esper Origins is cast from hand on turn 1 (Island surveilled into the
# graveyard) and flashed back on turn 3, entering transformed with a finality counter and its first lore counter.
# I: the top card, Lightning Bolt (kept there by the second surveil), is revealed; it is not a permanent card, so it stays
# on top of the library, where Bot1 draws it on turn 5.
# II (turn 5, after the draw step, CR 714.3b): "Add {G}{G}" - a triggered ability, not a mana ability, on the stack
# (the ruling); the two green are in Bot1's pool once it resolves.
# III (turn 7): "Other creatures you control get +2/+2 and gain trample until end of turn": Bot1's Llanowar Elves become a
# 3/3 with trample; Bot2's Ornithopter is not Bot1's and stays a 0/2 flier. With three lore counters and no chapter
# ability on the stack, the Saga is sacrificed (CR 714.4); the finality counter sends it to exile instead of the graveyard
# (CR 122.1h). On turn 8 the Elves are a 1/1 without trample again (CR 514.2).

